Offline French → Ukrainian dictionary of AI Ebook Reader
=========================================================

Built by tools/build_dict_fr_uk.py. Two files, each with its own licence (the two licences cannot be merged into one work,
so they are kept as separate files and the app reads them side by side):

dict/fr-uk.json — CC BY-SA 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/)
    French lemmas, forms, parts of speech, gender, frequency, Ukrainian meanings, set expressions. Adapted from:

    * Lexique 3.83 — New, B., Pallier, C., Brysbaert, M. & Ferrand, L. (2004). Lexique 2: A New French Lexical Database.
      Behavior Research Methods, Instruments, & Computers, 36(3), 516–524; New, B., Pallier, C., Ferrand, L. & Matos, R. (2001).
      Une base de données lexicales du français contemporain sur internet: LEXIQUE. L'Année Psychologique, 101, 447–462.
      http://www.lexique.org — CC BY-SA 4.0. (Read from the copy shipped in the pylexique 1.5.1 package on PyPI, same file.)
    * Wiktionary (https://en.wiktionary.org, https://fr.wiktionary.org), by its contributors — CC BY-SA 3.0 / 4.0 (and GFDL):
      - French headwords, their inflected forms and English senses, from the wiktextract extraction (Ylonen, T. (2022).
        Wiktextract: Wiktionary as Machine-Readable Structured Data. LREC 2022; https://kaikki.org) as published by the
        Wiktionary-Dictionaries project (https://github.com/Vuizur/Wiktionary-Dictionaries, commit be0cfb8d);
      - French → Ukrainian translations, through the Wiktionary-derived edges of ConceptNet 5.7 (Speer, R., Chin, J. & Havasi, C.
        (2017). ConceptNet 5.5: An Open Multilingual Graph of General Knowledge. AAAI 2017; https://conceptnet.io) — CC BY-SA 4.0.
      - French → Ukrainian translations of today's Wiktionary, from the wiktextract extracts of kaikki.org (the French Wiktionary,
        https://kaikki.org/frwiktionary/raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl.gz: its own «Traductions» into Ukrainian; the English Wiktionary,
        https://kaikki.org/dictionary/raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl.gz: French and Ukrainian words of the same translation table, kept
        only when the French word's own entry is glossed with that English word), downloaded 2026-10-30 (the SHA-256 of both files
        heads dict/src/wiktionary-fr-uk.tsv, where the pairs are kept so a build needs no access to kaikki.org) — CC BY-SA 4.0 / GFDL.
        Changes: stress marks removed, at most 4 meanings per word, every Ukrainian word checked against VESUM.
      Meanings taken from Wiktionary are marked "w" (source "wiktionary").
    * Meanings and set expressions written for this project (dict/src/*.tsv), marked "x" (source "written"); every Ukrainian word
      in them was checked against VESUM (below) and refused when VESUM marks it as non-standard.
    Changes: entries filtered, merged and re-encoded (front-coded form index), Ukrainian translations checked against VESUM.

dict/uk-forms.json — CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/) — NON-COMMERCIAL use only
    The forms (cases, numbers, genders, persons, tenses) of the Ukrainian words used by fr-uk.json, as endings, and the verb
    endings VESUM reads one way. Adapted from:

    * VESUM — Великий електронний словник української мови, dict_uk 6.8.6 (https://github.com/brown-uk/dict_uk),
      © Андрій Рисін, Василь Старко, команда БрУК — data under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 (the project's software is GPL 3.0; none of it
      is included here).
    Changes: only the words fr-uk.json needs, only the standard form of each slot, re-encoded as stem + endings.

The app works without dict/uk-forms.json (no agreement of a substituted word), so a commercial build can leave it out.
